# is needed; R2 is archival plus public access via data.civgraph.net.
data/census/

# Full territorial-transition sidecars: 153 MB of source QA artefacts.
# Regenerate with `python scripts/build_all_timeline_transition_sidecars.py`.
# The runtime uses the filtered overlays in data/timeline-transition-overlays/.
# The *.geojson line above already covered new ones; these four were committed
# before that rule existed, so they needed removing from the index explicitly.
data/timeline-transitions/

# Semantic graph: 4,604 files, 1.96 GB, pure build output. Regenerate with
# `npm run build:graph`; production serves it from R2 through
# functions/data/graph/[[path]].js. Untracked 2026-08-12 after verifying all
# 4,604 objects were present in the bucket.
data/graph/

# Browse indexes and detail pages: 2,386 files, 351 MB, regenerated by
# `npm run build:browse`. Served from R2 via functions/data/browse/[[path]].js.
#
# `data/browse/*` rather than `data/browse/`, because git cannot re-include a
# file inside an excluded DIRECTORY -- the negation below only works if the
# directory itself is still walked.
data/browse/*
# proni-roots.json is the exception and must stay in git. A regeneration test on
# 2026-08-12 rebuilt 2,278 of 2,386 files from clean; the 107 map details it did
# not rebuild are all legitimately stale (98 are hidden:true in the catalogue, 9
# are the retired eds-YYYY-province naming set), but this file is different:
# it is the only tracked file in an otherwise generated directory, and `npm run
# build` does not produce it -- scripts/build-proni-roots.mjs does, from the PRONI
# D1 database, and that is not part of the build. browse/browse.js fetches it with
# a silent `.catch(() => null)`, so if it were ever lost the only symptom would be
# a Browse section quietly going empty. `npm run check` now runs
# build-proni-roots.mjs --check so absence or staleness fails loudly instead.
!data/browse/proni-roots.json

# Dublin development-plan scans: 12 files, 167 MB, already on R2 and already
