data/quarantine/

# Source books — R2 is the canonical store, Internet Archive is the public mirror.
#
# 365 MB of Hansard OCR (213 MB) and NI Acts/SRO PDFs (152 MB), uploaded 2026-08-23 to
# s3://boundaries-data/data/books/ and to archive.org items civgraph-ni-hansard-1921-1945
# and civgraph-ni-acts-sro-1921-1932. books.json points `file` and `markdownFile` at
# https://data.civgraph.net/..., and check:book-files verifies every remote URL is on
# that host and under an allowlisted prefix.
#
# UNTRACKED rather than only .cfignore'd because .cfignore did not exclude them: both
# directories still served 200 from Pages after two confirmed deploys (the same commit's
# books.json change WAS live), while `scripts/` and `ocr_output/` in the same file are
# correctly excluded. Rather than keep guessing at the matcher, this removes them from
# the build input entirely -- which is also what stops the pack growing, since these were
# its largest churning blobs.
#
# They remain in git history, on R2 and on Internet Archive. Nothing is lost.
data/books/markdown/
data/books/legislation/

# Generated D1 import, 16.7 MB, rebuilt by scripts/build-persons-d1-import.mjs.
# Tracked no more than catalogue-d1-import.sql is: it is derived from the browse index.
data/database/persons-d1-import.sql
data/database/register-interests-d1-import.sql
data/database/sources-d1-import.sql


